From 403bbd059726c5a7629243c52db49737839aa2b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GNB Build <palimpseste@quidam.eu>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:29:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] feat(companion): add local WiFi-config contact
 ("w_<node name>")

Lets a companion app configure wifi_ssid/wifi_pwd/wifi_enabled via an
ordinary chat message to a synthetic contact named "w_<node name>", using
the existing "key:value" syntax already used by CMD_SET_CUSTOM_VAR
(wifi_ssid:MyNetwork, wifi_pwd:..., wifi_enabled:1). Never touches the
radio: intercepted in the CMD_SEND_TXT_MSG handler right after the
(successful) contact lookup, before any sendMessage()/sendCommandData()
call.

Same underlying principle as ZephCore's v-contact (synthetic pubkey
derived by hashing our own identity, so nothing is ever actually sent
over LoRa), adapted to this codebase: since BaseChatMesh's contact table
has no virtual-injection hook, the contact is a genuine addContact()
entry instead, ensured idempotently at every boot (ensureWifiConfigContact,
called right after loadContacts() in begin()), including keeping its
display name in sync if the node is renamed later.

- MyMesh.h: new private members (_wifi_contact_key, ensureWifiConfigContact,
  isWifiConfigContact, trySetWifiConfigVar, queueLocalConfigReply), all
  gated by DUAL_BLE_WIFI/EXCLUSIVE_BLE_WIFI like the existing wifi_ssid/
  wifi_pwd/wifi_enabled handling.
- MyMesh.cpp: the three new functions; CMD_SET_CUSTOM_VAR's existing
  wifi_ssid/wifi_pwd/wifi_enabled branch now calls the shared
  trySetWifiConfigVar() instead of duplicating the field-set logic;
  CMD_SEND_TXT_MSG fabricates the same SENT-ack hash a real send would
  produce (from the untouched text, before splitting on ':'), plus an
  immediate PUSH_CODE_SEND_CONFIRMED (nothing is ever in flight to wait
  for), then queues a local reply via queueLocalConfigReply() (mirrors
  queueMessage() without dereferencing a real mesh::Packet*).

Status: compiles clean for heltec_tracker_v2_companion_radio_ble_wifi_exclusive
(RAM 63.0%, Flash 51.2%). Never flashed or tested on real hardware yet --
beta build in builds/beta-releases/, not builds/releases/.
